{
  "rules": [
    "When the model forecasts a steady upward trend while recent history shows high volatility or consolidation, apply a downward correction of 5-10% to account for mean reversion risks.",
    "If sentiment spikes (e.g., >0.20) immediately preceding a forecast horizon, reduce the projected upside by 8-12% as models often overestimate momentum during short-term rallies.",
    "In volatile regimes where true outcomes exhibit sharp reversals (e.g., Example 3 and 4), apply a volatility buffer: subtract 5% from the first week's forecast and add 5% to the last week's forecast to capture mean reversion.",
    "When sentiment history shows mixed signals (alternating 0.00 and 0.20) but price action is trending up, assume the model ignores underlying uncertainty; reduce the forecasted peak by 10%.",
    "If the true outcome deviates >5% from the model's linear projection within the first 7 days, reverse the trend direction for the remaining horizon to avoid overshooting."
  ]
}
